DESCRIPTION:<p>Modeling LLVM's distinct metadata in MLIR is non-trivial and
  may require some extension of MLIR core. Two different proposals have been
  discussed in <a href="https://discourse.llvm.org/t/rfc-use-attributes-to-m
 odel-distinct-llvm-metadata-nodes/69924"><u>https://discourse.llvm.org/t/rf
 c-use-attributes-to-model-distinct-llvm-metadata-nodes/69924</u>. A design 
 discussion may be helpful to converge to a final design</a> (Tobias Gysi)<b
 r></p><p><a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1y2YlcOVMPocQjSFi3X6gY
 GRjA0onyqr41ilXji10phw/edit#">Agenda for future meetings</a></p><p><a href=
 "https://us06web.zoom.us/j/85151090498?pwd=QUdqUGNETzVxMTBnM1p4UDVrdVVKUT09
 ">Zoom Meeting Link</a></p><p>Meeting ID: 851 5109 0498<br>Passcode: 828404
 </p><p><br></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250102T153447Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:MLIR Open Meeting: RFC on Distinct Attributes
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
