BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260521T170000Z
DTEND:20260521T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20261027T013714Z
UID:1u19043718g4j499js4nv1osfs@google.com
CREATED:20260419T163203Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>In May\, <a href="https://github.com/bruno-ah-um" target="_b
 lank">Bruno Caballero</a> will show us how to target hardware accelerators 
 from Java with MLIR based on <a href="https://github.com/bruno-ah-um/openjd
 k-babylon-mlir-tosa" target="_blank">his fork of the OpenJDK Project Babylo
 n</a>.<br><br>Bruno leads the Java Virtual Machines Engineering team at <a 
 href="http://www.microdoc.com" target="_blank">MicroDoc</a>\, which develop
 s JVMs and maintains ports across various processors and operating systems.
 <br><br><b>Abstract:</b> In this talk\, we’ll explore a toy project that tr
 anslates Java code into MLIR for the TOSA dialect\, which is used for AI an
 d accelerator workloads. We’ll briefly introduce current approaches (e.g.\,
  TornadoVM and Babylon/HAT)\, before looking at how this project reuses exi
 sting compiler infrastructure instead of building new backends. Finally\, w
 e’ll touch on whether DSLs should be embedded in general-purpose languages 
 like Java or designed as standalone languages.<br><span><br><b>How to find 
 us:</b> Go through the gate on <a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/8yydMT1yZdQ
 8s3Qr9">Rungestr. 20</a> and straight to the 2. courtyard (not the riversid
 e!). Find the green door on the right of the courtyard\, ring at LLVM and g
 o up to the 2rd floor. In case you know: it's right above <a href="https://
 c-base.org/">c-base</a>.</span><br><br>Small snacks and drinks will be avai
 lable. There is always space for outside topics and discussions. If you hav
 e specific questions\, please bring them. Looking forward to meeting everyo
 ne again!<br><br>More RSVPs: <a href="https://www.meetup.com/llvm-social-be
 rlin/events/314246966/">https://www.meetup.com/llvm-social-berlin/events/31
 4246966/</a></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260503T161200Z
LOCATION:Rungestraße 20\, 10179 Berlin\, Germany
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:LLVM Meetup Berlin (Germany)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
