UID:7t4sh64uemlj76fq9qta8j1jkt_R20230309T170000@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20230309T090000
CREATED:20230129T225512Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><span>Convolution is one of the most common linear algebra o
 perations for machine-learning applications. With the increasingly importan
 t compiler integration into such frameworks\, improving performance in code
 -generated implementations of convolution is key for the future. In this ta
 lk\, </span><span>Victor Ferrari (UNICAMP)</span><span> presents a new conv
 olution approach for MLIR which improves performance when compared to the t
 raditional Im2Col + GEMM method used in the linalg dialect and many other p
 laces.</span></p><p><br></p><p><a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/
 1y_9f1AbfgcoVdJh4_aM6-BaSHvrHl8zuA5G4jv_94K8/edit#">Agenda for future meeti
 ngs</a></p><p><a href="https://us06web.zoom.us/j/85151090498?pwd=QUdqUGNETz
 VxMTBnM1p4UDVrdVVKUT09">Zoom Meeting Link</a></p><p>Meeting ID: 851 5109 04
 98<br>Passcode: 828404</p><p><br></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250102T153447Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:MLIR Open Meeting: Integrating Convolution Optimization into MLIR t
 o Improve Performance Beyond Im2Col+GEMM
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
