BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260521T170000Z
DTEND:20260521T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20261027T013714Z
UID:2vvblbo515th38opqsracdde24@google.com
CREATED:20260425T093801Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>In May\, <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://githu
 b.com/bruno-ah-um&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw
 0EWFQvlcfRqSTLsSesgxnh" target="_blank">Bruno Caballero</a> will show us ho
 w to target hardware accelerators from Java with MLIR based on <a href="htt
 ps://www.google.com/url?q=https://github.com/bruno-ah-um/openjdk-babylon-ml
 ir-tosa&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw0GWkZLB6bK
 SlftyAe8vFJG" target="_blank">his fork of the OpenJDK Project Babylon</a>.<
 br><br>Bruno leads the Java Virtual Machines Engineering team at <a href="h
 ttps://www.google.com/url?q=http://www.microdoc.com&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=c
 alendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw29Hm-uoBVjz6cZaxW1FJCq" target="_blank">M
 icroDoc</a>\, which develops JVMs and maintains ports across various proces
 sors and operating systems.<br><br><b>Abstract:</b> In this talk\, we’ll ex
 plore a toy project that translates Java code into MLIR for the TOSA dialec
 t\, which is used for AI and accelerator workloads. We’ll briefly introduce
  current approaches (e.g.\, TornadoVM and Babylon/HAT)\, before looking at 
 how this project reuses existing compiler infrastructure instead of buildin
 g new backends. Finally\, we’ll touch on whether DSLs should be embedded in
  general-purpose languages like Java or designed as standalone languages.<b
 r><span><br><b>How to find us:</b> Go through the gate on <a href="https://
 www.google.com/url?q=https://maps.app.goo.gl/8yydMT1yZdQ8s3Qr9&amp\;sa=D&am
 p\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw2BzrCMnWtjHU3wJd3-uMvf" target
 ="_blank">Rungestr. 20</a> and straight to the 2. courtyard (not the rivers
 ide!). Find the green door on the right of the courtyard\, ring at LLVM and
  go up to the 2rd floor. In case you know: it&#39\;s right above <a href="h
 ttps://www.google.com/url?q=https://c-base.org/&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calen
 dar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw2jRSEor9gVKXWWTC20b16d" target="_blank">c-bas
 e</a>.</span><br><br>Small snacks and drinks will be available. There is al
 ways space for outside topics and discussions. If you have specific questio
 ns\, please bring them. Looking forward to meeting everyone again!<br><br>M
 ore RSVPs: <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.meetup.com/llv
 m-social-berlin/events/314246966/&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2
 &amp\;usg=AOvVaw1kUpAKYqDI0yiPvgZ5YSJi" target="_blank">https://www.meetup.
 com/llvm-social-berlin/events/314246966/</a></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260426T094944Z
LOCATION:Rungestraße 20\, 10179 Berlin\, Germany
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:LLVM Meetup Berlin (Germany)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
