 031</a>\n</p><p/><p>\n  <b>Agenda</b>\n</p><ul>\n  <li>Introductions</li>\n
   <li>Problem Statement</li>\n  <li>Recap of current work &amp\; investigat
 ion\n    <ul>\n      <li>Meta &amp\; Google can each describe</li></ul></li
 >\n  <li>Alignment on direction</li>\n  <li>Work in progress</li>\n  <li>Ne
 xt meeting time discussion</li></ul><p>\nHigh level organization: meeting n
 otes\, public facing website and documentation\n</p><p>\nOther ideas to dis
 cuss:\n</p><p>\n* \n</p><p>\n  <a href="https://discourse.llvm.org/t/rfc-an
 -opt-in-cmake-option-for-64-bit-source-location/87538">https://discourse.ll
 vm.org/t/rfc-an-opt-in-cmake-option-for-64-bit-source-location/87538</a>\n<
 /p><p>\n* tls 64bit relocations (__tls_get_addr)\n</p><p/><p>\nAttendees mu
 st adhere to the LLVM Code of Conduct\n</p><p>\n(\n  <a href="https://llvm.
 org/docs/CodeOfConduct.html">https://llvm.org/docs/CodeOfConduct.html</a>).
  For any Code of Conduct reports\, please contact the organizers and also e
